+### Operation contract source bounds
+
+`yunka change plan --intent contract|both` and `change begin` resolve exact editable protobuf files from the existing Operation's declaration and transitive request/response message, map-value and enum references. A shared Service importing unrelated DTO modules does not make those modules editable. The read-only Context's `sourceFiles` remains a full import closure; `declarationFiles` is the narrower source projection. Neither Context field issues mutation authority by itself.
+
+Whenever a Change Contract or ChangeSet contains an actual `.proto` delta, `change check`, `change set check`, and `change verify` independently compile the immutable Git base and current sources. Reconciliation reports the `operation-declaration-sources/v1` policy in `contractSources`; single-change and ChangeSet check reports use schema v2. The existing Change Contract v1 and ChangeSet v2 input protocols remain supported. No new source mapping is persisted or hand-maintained.
+
+The gate intersects declared paths with base Operation/DTO provenance. It rejects unrelated protobuf files even when path arrays are expanded or a current DTO is changed to reference an unrelated pre-existing type. Canonical message/enum field changes outside the allowed type graph are also rejected inside an otherwise allowed file. New reachable DTOs may be authored in already authorized files; shared reachable DTOs are admitted. Existing/new Operation subjects and multiple subjects reuse the same gate. Direct source changes to permission, tenant, transaction, composition and other canonical semantics are checked using the existing semantic evaluator, even when generated JSON has not been refreshed.
+
+Protobuf rename/copy destinations do not acquire authority automatically: both the Git path envelope and base-bound source set must admit them. An unplanned source move fails rather than silently reassigning ownership; perform a separately bounded structural migration and start a fresh Operation task. Unknown/broken/missing base or current inputs fail closed. Required explicit compiler includes are supported by `change plan`, `change begin`, `change check`, and `change set check` through `--protoc` / repeatable `--proto-path`; inventory include order remains in `sourceSets[].protoPaths`.
+
+The immutable baseline is materialized from raw Git tree/blob objects into a private temporary directory, without changing a checkout, following replacement objects, applying export attributes, running historical code or fetching submodules. Canonical sources and inventory configuration must exist in the chosen Git baseline. Project-external includes remain external read-only compiler inputs. Implementation-only deltas retain the non-compiling quick path.
+
+This is a deterministic source/declaration guard, not a business-ontology judgment, token-minimal source slicer or filesystem sandbox. Declaration comparison covers the compiler's canonical Message/Enum model; it does not claim AST-level coverage of every custom protobuf option or comment. `change set check` still is not a substitute for full `yunka check`, Go tests, API compatibility policy, or runtime qualification. Trusted task issuance still owns the baseline/subject identities. Generated outputs remain subject to existing drift/ownership checks, and no test or runtime gate is removed.
+
